--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Lazy-wave armoured power cable restrained in torsion at the hang-off and free to twist at the anchor, heaving 36 s
-- The 80 m Gulf of Mexico cable of lozon_gomex80_power_cable_motion.dat (64 elements, the 3 m,
-- 12 s hang-off heave of data/lozon/gomex80_heave_3m_12s_dt005.txt), with ILLUSTRATIVE torsion
-- properties of a single-armoured cable: GJ = 50 kN.m^2, a torque-tension coupling K = 3.0 MN.m
-- (T = EA eps + K tau, M = GJ tau + K eps, K^2 < EA GJ) and a torsional damping of 5 % of each
-- element's critical value (the GJ column GJ|K|Bt, Bt = -0.05). The hang-off is clamped (Rigid)
-- and restrained in torsion (TorsStiffness Rigid); the anchor end has no END CONNECTIONS row, so
-- it is pinned and free to twist, as on a swivel. The free end carries no torque: in statics the
-- line has none, and the stretch alone twists it, Twist1 = -sum (K/GJ)(l - L) over the elements:
-- -5.6 deg here, the stretch being that of the reduced axial stiffness EA - K^2/GJ of a line free
-- to twist. Under the heave the tension, and with it the stretch, oscillates (Twist1 between
-- -7.6 and -3.7 deg): the twist follows through torsional waves carried by the polar inertia
-- Irn (m r^2/2 of each section) that reflect at the free end, and the restrained hang-off takes
-- their torque, Torq1N1. Twist1 is the turn of the free anchor end against the hang-off frame
-- carried along the line.
